": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "without", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170413 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/6b4d617df080cef71cd8f4b041601cf47ce0edf3/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nApplying fixes:\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nAll 16 tests now pass with `python3 -m unittest`. The earlier run counted 15 because `test_search` couldn't be imported, so its two real tests never ran.\n\n**The three reads you asked for:**\n- **(a)** Reading the `catalog/` directory listed 8 entries: `__init__.py`, `books.py`, `factory.py`, `fees.py`, `inventory.py`, `members.py`, `search.py`, `text.py`.\n- **(b)** `books.py` with offset 0, limit 5 returned lines 1\u20135: the docstring through `def __init__(...)`.\n- **(c)** `books.py` with offset 3, limit 5 returned lines 4\u20138, from `class Book:` through `self.year = year`. So for this tool the offset is effectively the 1-based line to start at, not a 0-based offset: offset 0 and offset 1 would both start at line 1.\n\n**Fixes (only files in `catalog/` changed; tests untouched):**\n- `catalog/search.py:3`: the import pointed at a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`); it now imports `normalize` from `catalog.text`.\n- `catalog/books.py:22`: `parse_book` left the year as a string, which also broke `age()`. It now converts it with `int(year)`.